Why ShareAlike
--------------
The benchmark datasets are built from GTDB release 226, published under CC BY-SA 4.0. A derived
dataset must carry the same licence, so the whole data tree does.

Upstream sources and their terms
--------------------------------
GTDB r226       CC BY-SA 4.0
                Parks DH et al. GTDB: an ongoing census of bacterial and archaeal
                diversity. Nucleic Acids Res (2022). https://gtdb.ecogenomic.org
Rfam 15.1       CC0 (public domain dedication)
                Covariance models RF01959 (archaeal SSU) and RF00177 (bacterial SSU).
                Ontiveros-Palacios N et al. Nucleic Acids Res (2025).
Infernal 1.1.5  BSD 3-Clause. Used as a container, not redistributed here.
RAxML Grove     No licence is stated upstream (database at
                https://cme.h-its.org/exelixis/material/raxmlgrove/). The simulated
                control keeps one tree taken from it, with its model parameters, for
                scientific reuse with attribution.
                Höhler D et al. Bioinformatics 38(6):1741 (2022).

If you reuse the data, cite this benchmark and the sources above.
